== 3. g3 ==
White prepares to fianchetto their bishop. White chooses a [[Chess Opening Theory/1. d4/1...Nf6/2. c4/2...e6/3. g3|Catalan-style]] set up, an approach that combines c4 and d4 with a king's side fianchetto. 

This is a less common move order. Black usually develops their knight next, [[/3...Nf6|'''3...Nf6''']], and the same Catalan position is reached as if the game had played out in the order 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. g3 d5. 

